{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, as HaShem rejoiced over you to do you good and to multiply you.</b> He Himself does not rejoice in calamity, but others do rejoice. And from this verse is hinted the end [of days] that is written in Daniel: ״ומעת הוסר התמיד ולתת שקוץ שומם ימים אלף מאתים ותשעים״. This is what it says: והיה כאשר שש ה׳ עליכם להטיב אתכם — in the wilderness and in the land of Israel, when the Shekhinah was with you; ולהרבות אתכם — in Egypt, as it is said ״וירבו ויעצמו״, which is one thousand two hundred and ninety. These are the years of the Egyptian exile, and furthermore from the exodus from Egypt until the House was built, as it is written ״ויהי בשמונים וארבע מאות שנה לצאת בני ישראל מארץ מצרים ויבן את הבית לה׳״. And furthermore the years the First House stood, which is the numerical value of בזא״ת יבא אהרן — behold, the total of all is one thousand seven hundred and ninety [קק״צ]. So too the exile will last, as it is said ״כי למועד מועדים וחצי וגו׳ תכלינה כל אלה״. למועד הראשון — 'an appointed time' is explained as 'a set time,' as in למועד הזה. מועדים וחצי — that is, two set times, like מועד צאתך ממצרים — like the two set times of Egypt. וחצי — means half of the second מועדים, that is, a third מועד. And behold they are three מועדים, just as they were in Egypt according to the verse ״ומושב בני ישראל אשר ישבו במצרים שלשים וארבע מאות שנה״. And three times this [430] yields one thousand two hundred and ninety, and then the exile will end. And likewise the other verse says: ״ויתיהבון בידיה עד עדן עדנים ופלג עדן״. And if He had wanted, He could have said explicitly 'three מועדים,' but He wanted to conceal His words. And here Moses hinted at this in the Torah, and so Hosea said: ״וענתה שמה כימי נעוריה וכיום עלותה מארץ מצרים״. וענתה — in the sense of dwelling, as in ״וענה איים בארמנותיו״ — כימי נעוריה, that is, the exile of her youth, which is the Egyptian exile; וכיום עלותה מארץ מצרים — this is from the exodus from Egypt until the Temple was destroyed, and this is one thousand two hundred and ninety as explained above. Thus it is found written in the Torah, repeated in the Prophets, and triplicated in the Writings. And the later end, as it is written at the end of Daniel — ״אשרי המחכה ויגיע לימים אלף שלש מאות שלשים וחמשה״ — is hinted in the portion אתם נצבים, where it is written ״ואנכי הסתר אסתיר פני מהם ביום ההוא וגו׳״ — הסת״ר אסתי״ר has the gematria of one thousand three hundred thirty-six, with the help of Shaddai; but the Messiah will come, may it be His will, at the end of one thousand seven hundred and ninety [קק״צ], which is forty-five years before. But we do not know from where the count begins, so that we may know when it ends. And likewise we find with the end of Egypt: the Holy One, blessed be He, said ״וענו אותם ארבע מאות שנה״, and this was said thirty years before Isaac was born, for Abraham was seventy years old at that time and one hundred when Isaac was born — behold, thirty years between this and that. And the tribe of Ephraim counted four hundred from the covenant between the pieces, and they erred by thirty, and the men of Gath killed them, as it is written in Chronicles. And there are those who began the count from when they went down to Egypt, and they erred. And there are those who counted from when the servitude began, and they erred. And the truth was that the four hundred years began from when Isaac was born, but it was not known with certainty until they went out of Egypt. And likewise regarding the Babylonian exile, the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Jeremiah ״לפי מלאת לבבל שבעים שנה״, and Belshazzar calculated and erred, and Ahasuerus counted and erred, as is explained in the first chapter of Megillah. So too this end — perhaps it begins from the year of the abolition of the daily offering in the days of Hyrcanus and Aristobulus, as is taught at the end of tractate Sotah: the Rabbai taught — when the kings of the Hasmonean house besieged one another, Hyrcanus was on the outside and Aristobulus on the inside, etc., and then the daily offering was abolished. And when the Messiah comes speedily in our days, then the matters will become clear and clarified, and then we will know retroactively from where it began. And the Rav Bekhor Shor says that this end is hinted in the alphabet of תשר״ק, for תשר״ק equals one thousand; צפע״״ס equals three hundred; and then נמל״ך — the kingdom will be handed over to Israel, for the Messiah has already come ten years before the end of one thousand seven hundred and ninety [קק״צ]; יטח״ז equals thirty-four — behold the beginning of the thirty-fifth year, and this is one thousand three hundred thirty-five. And afterward יטחז — the הד״ג ב״א — the delight comes, when all the world will be conquered under the hand of Israel, that is, the Leviathan will come to make a feast for the righteous."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The text contains many abbreviations involving gematria (e.g., קק״צ = 1790, יטח״ז = 34, יטחז, הד״ג ב״א, נמל״ך) whose expanded meanings are uncertain; these are rendered from context but remain tentative. The reading הד״ג ב״א is obscure and possibly corrupt. The phrase כג״ה appears to be an abbreviation for כגונח הוא or similar; rendered here as 'may it be His will' from context. The צפע״״ס abbreviation is tentatively resolved to צפ״ן ע״״ס = 300."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:47.093522533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}